5. Provide the complete corresponding source code of the Modified Work to each recipient, without additional charge.
6. Do not impose additional legal or technical restrictions that prevent recipients from exercising the rights granted under this License.

For purposes of this section, complete corresponding source code includes the human-readable source files and reasonably necessary build or installation instructions, excluding independent third-party dependencies available separately.

Merely running the Software on a server, without distributing copies or a Modified Work, does not trigger a requirement to publish source code.

A separate program that merely communicates with the Software through ordinary interfaces does not automatically become a Modified Work solely because of that communication.

